 ],
 "says": "A person with no Team installs the knowledge package shipped in the product through the add_published_package route (source.revision.admit), naming the exact revision by the digest of the shipped manifest. The owner commits it and returns that same manifest and a provenance whose origin is the product-supplied package, whose acceptance is not_accepted and whose content-review statement is kept as an approval claim with stated_only support, never as an acceptance. Resolving an exact member (reference.resolve) returns the same manifest, whose member digest is the member the reference names, and the same provenance. Asking a question against that exact revision (knowledge.question.ask) returns a view whose members are the package's bytes in the person's own layer, cited to that revision. Nothing here adopts the package for a Team, records a Team acceptance, or gives it a priority: the provenance has no priority field and the view places it only in the layer it was installed into.",
 "spec_sha256": "ecad81d5a857af00d38ab035589d12d323a6db3a93eaf7993d2e857af43a7057",
 "steps": [
